# Regex basic literal roundtrip

Verifies plain regex literals keep their source text through parsing and
printing: `/hello/` denotes a literal match and `/cat|dog/` an alternation,
and both print back verbatim.

>>> source
word: regex = /hello/
print(word)
alternation: regex = /cat|dog/
print(alternation)

<<< stdout
/hello/
/cat|dog/

<<< stderr
